-SEDOM is an organization that provides criteria for coding hospital malnutrition.,2\r\n12880,CSCN,\"CSCN, or the Canadian Society for Clinical Nutrition, is a Canadian organization dedicated to providing clinical guidelines for nutrition in critically ill patients. The society emphasizes the importance of enteral nutrition over parenteral nutrition for this patient population, advocating for practices that enhance patient care and recovery through appropriate nutritional support.\",2\r\n13209,ASOCIACIÓN AMERICANA DE NEUROCIRUGÍA,The Asociación Americana de Neurocirugía provides guidelines for the nutritional support of patients with traumatic brain injuries (TCE).,1\r\n12903,NUTRIC,NUTRIC is a scoring system used to assess the risk of malnutrition in patients.,1\r\n15507,GAUDERER MW,\"Gauderer MW is an author who has contributed to the field of enteral nutrition, particularly in the context of pediatric care.\",1\r\n15508,BAKER SS,Baker SS is an editor and author in pediatric nutrition support literature.,1\r\n8063,RBP,\"RBP, or retinol-binding protein, is a crucial protein that plays a significant role in the transport of vitamin A within the body. It binds to retinol, which is essential for nutritional assessment and overall health. RBP is characterized by its short half-life, indicating that it is rapidly metabolized in the body. This protein is vital for maintaining adequate levels of vitamin A, which is important for various physiological functions, including vision, immune response, and cellular communication.\",2\r\n3299,DENT E,A researcher who has conducted systematic reviews on nutritional screening tools for older adults.,2\r\n12646,THORELL A,Thorell A is a researcher who contributed to the guidelines for perioperative care in bariatric surgery.,3\r\n13183,TORONTO EQUATION,\"The Toronto equation is a formula suggested for calculating energy requirements in burned patients, based on regression analysis from indirect calorimetry studies.\",2\r\n13185,BURNED